        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: genus, naming system\n- Species: Parnassius nordmanni\n- Plants: Corydalis, C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, C. emanueli\n- Places: Caucasus\n\nFacts:\n- Corydalis and Abies, a relative of fir, are classified as genera in the naming system.\n- Parnassius nordmanni is a high-altitude butterfly found in the Caucasus.\n- The larva of Parnassius nordmanni feeds on Corydalis species, including C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, and C. emanueli.",
