        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Corydalis, Cedrus, firs\n- Animals: Parnassius nordmanni\n- Families: Papaveraceae, Pinaceae\n- Topics: plant taxonomy, larval host plants, phylogenetic relationships\n\nFacts:\n- Corydalis is a genus of about 470 annual and perennial herbaceous plant species in the family Papaveraceae.\n- Corydalis is native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere and the high mountains of tropical eastern Africa.\n- Cedrus, commonly called cedar, is a genus of coniferous trees in the family Pinaceae.\n- Firs are most closely related to the genus Cedrus.\n- The larva of Parnassius nordmanni feeds on Corydalis species including C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, and C. emanueli.",
